{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>For, etc.</b> Because He said \"and your widowhood\" — since the nations taunt Israel that they have no king — HaShem said: like a forsaken woman you were, and broken of spirit, who was abandoned by her husband. Yet her husband lives, as He said, \"for your Maker is your husband.\" The word עצובת is an adjective, not a verb form; if it is on its [verbal] pattern, therefore it is written, \"YHWH called you back, like a wife forsaken and afflicted in spirit, like a wife of one's youth when she is rejected, says HaShem.\" And so it was:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 54, :notes {0 "The comment cites Isaiah 54:4 (וחרפת אלמנותיך), then Isaiah 54:5 (כי בועליך עושיך), then Isaiah 54:6 itself; the final וכן היית (\"and so it was\") may be a gloss or colophon."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:30.124353448Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}